# Safety case of the course robot's arm, version for the SS402 build (files from labs F11-18..F11-22).
G|G0|-|any|the course robot's arm is acceptably safe to operate in the lab under supervision
C|C0|G0|course robot: wheeled base with a small arm; modes operate, teach, charge, maintenance
C|C2|G0|scope: the arm's hazards H2, H3, H4, H5; the base (H1, H6, H7) has its own case
C|C1|G0|acceptably safe = every hazard of the hazard log is mitigated to its course target (CT)
A|A0|G0|the robot is operated only in the university lab, by trained learners, with a supervisor
S|S0|G0|argue over every hazard identified in the hazard log
G|G1|S0|any|the hazard log is complete for the robot's modes
E|E1|G1|analysis|../F11-19/hazard_log.out|0 findings: the log passes the course's completeness checks
G|G2|S0|any|H2 overspeed: the speed monitor stops the arm before it reaches the hazardous speed
E|E2|G2|sim|../F11-18/safety_function.out|scenarios with a hazardous speed: 0
G|G3|S0|any|H3 e-stop: the arm is at rest before the relay removes drive power
S|S3|G3|argue over the software ramp and the hard-wired chain separately
G|G31|S3|sim|the control thread brings the arm to rest within the relay delay
E|E31|G31|sim|../F11-21/estop_fixed.out|e-stop handled in: control;software brought it to rest before the relay
G|G32|S3|hw|the hard-wired chain removes drive power on the real robot within the relay delay
U|G32|untested on hardware in this build: needs the robot, a timer on the drive enable and a supervisor
G|G4|S0|any|H5 unexpected start: after a stop the arm cannot start by itself
E|E4|G4|sim|../F11-21/watchdog_test.out|T4 the trip is latched;T5 reset refused while e-stop pressed;ALL TESTS PASSED
G|G5|S0|any|every safety requirement is traced to a passing test on this build, except G32's test
